# Git target branch

- Default branch for this repo is **`main`**.
- When the user asks to commit and/or push, work on **`main`** (checkout or create it if needed), commit there, and **`git push -u origin main`**.
- Do not open long-lived feature branches or push only to `master` unless the user explicitly asks for a different branch or a PR workflow.
- If local `master` still exists, keep it aligned with `main` after pushes (`git push origin HEAD:master` only when needed to avoid drift), but treat **`main` as the source of truth**.
